.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-keys - Generate signing keys locally and manage them in the OS keychain


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 keys [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a new wallet key pair locally with 'rail0 keys generate' (offline; the
private key is printed once and stored nowhere).

.PP
Save signing keys in the OS keychain and reference them as "@name" on the
--private-key flag (e.g. 'rail0 payments create -p @payer'), instead of pasting
a raw key or exporting RAIL0_PRIVATE_KEY.

.PP
The secret never touches the config file or your shell history. Backends: macOS
Keychain, Windows Credential Manager, Linux Secret Service. On a system without
one (e.g. headless Linux) add/rm/address return an error; use --private-key /
RAIL0_PRIVATE_KEY there.

.PP
There is no listing of saved keys, by design: a keychain cannot be enumerated,
so a list could only report a copy of the names kept alongside the config — and
that copy drifts. Ask about one key at a time with 'rail0 keys address \&',
which reads the keychain itself and cannot go stale.

.PP
\&'rail0 keys balance \&' reads an address's balance straight from the
chain's public RPC endpoints.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for keys


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 keys generate
  rail0 keys add payer
  rail0 payments create -p @payer …
  rail0 keys address payer
  rail0 keys balance payer --chain arc
  rail0 keys rm payer
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0(1)\fP, \fBrail0-keys-add(1)\fP, \fBrail0-keys-address(1)\fP, \fBrail0-keys-balance(1)\fP, \fBrail0-keys-generate(1)\fP, \fBrail0-keys-rm(1)\fP
